WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.545
Welcome to Between, a dating laboratory with twenty five entirely fictional people.

00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:07.830
Each has two authored source profiles and a personal agent.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:13.688
The experiment runs all three hundred unique pairings, giving every person twenty four ranked connections.

00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:15.824
Start with the people, not the scores.

00:00:15.824 --> 00:00:18.890
You can browse by city or search for a shared interest.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.800
Here is the complete input flow.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.352
Add a person, paste their LinkedIn and public Instagram fixture links, and read the sources.

00:00:26.352 --> 00:00:31.128
These example addresses identify fictional documents, not real social accounts.

00:00:31.128 --> 00:00:33.277
The analysis opens a profile first.

00:00:33.277 --> 00:00:36.321
Maya values curiosity, kindness, and independence.

00:00:36.321 --> 00:00:41.396
Her hobbies, needs, and relationship intention come from explicit source statements.

00:00:41.396 --> 00:00:43.732
Nothing is hidden behind a personality label.

00:00:43.732 --> 00:00:50.118
Open the LinkedIn fixture to inspect the original document, then the Instagram fixture to read Maya's interests and needs.

00:00:50.118 --> 00:00:52.350
Each extracted statement keeps its source.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.167
Missing information stays unknown.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:01:00.345
The agent represents what the person actually said, rather than guessing romantic needs from a career or a photograph.

00:01:00.345 --> 00:01:03.416
Now Maya's agent meets Leo's at a neighborhood cafe.

00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:06.015
The first turn identifies shared interests.

00:01:06.015 --> 00:01:10.031
Leo's agent responds with a stated need and asks about social time.

00:01:10.031 --> 00:01:12.689
Maya's agent adapts and proposes a schedule.

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.520
Leo responds to that proposal.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.418
Finally, the agents check their relationship intentions directly.

00:01:18.418 --> 00:01:22.552
You can pause, step through, or open the explanation behind any turn.

00:01:22.552 --> 00:01:25.575
A different pairing produces a different conversation.

00:01:25.575 --> 00:01:27.815
Samir prefers quiet, predictable plans.

00:01:27.815 --> 00:01:30.390
Inez prefers a spontaneous, social afternoon.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:34.589
Their agents negotiate a fixed start time with an optional group activity.

00:01:34.589 --> 00:01:37.389
But Samir wants commitment and Inez is exploring.

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:39.684
The harness preserves that disagreement.

00:01:39.684 --> 00:01:44.779
It caps the score instead of pretending a clever compromise resolves different intentions.

00:01:44.779 --> 00:01:48.527
Only after the profiles and conversations do we compare connections.

00:01:48.527 --> 00:01:51.833
Every person receives a ranking from their own perspective.

00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:57.345
Open Why this fit to inspect values, interests, intentions, rhythm, social energy, and negotiation.

00:01:57.345 --> 00:01:58.998
Different cities are flagged.

00:01:58.998 --> 00:02:03.573
These are transparent heuristic scores, not probabilities of relationship success.

00:02:03.573 --> 00:02:06.108
You can switch people and replay any pairing.

00:02:06.108 --> 00:02:07.505
The demo is also editable.

00:02:07.505 --> 00:02:14.543
Supply two new fictional source documents using the labeled format, and the app creates a new agent and recalculates all pairings.

00:02:14.543 --> 00:02:16.692
Custom characters stay in this browser.

00:02:16.692 --> 00:02:20.883
Export downloads the sources, analyses, conversations, and rankings together.

00:02:20.883 --> 00:02:25.665
The default twenty five person experiment is always available without entering anything.

00:02:25.665 --> 00:02:28.975
Between uses an inspectable, rule based agent harness.

00:02:28.975 --> 00:02:32.225
No language model or live social scraper is claimed.

00:02:32.225 --> 00:02:40.072
It is a complete fictional simulation: two sources, an evidence backed profile, visible agent dates, and personalized rankings.

00:02:40.072 --> 00:02:42.279
The website works without API keys.

00:02:42.279 --> 00:02:43.689
A little less swiping.

00:02:43.689 --> 00:02:45.283
A little more connection.

